  "details": "<p>Richard Talbert provides commentary on the interpretation of this place name in the <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://www.cambridge.org/us/talbert/talbertdatabase/TPPlace423.html\" target=\"_self\" title=\"Name: Babylonia Feature type: symbol Ab2, named  Segment grid: 8C4\">database</a> accompanying his 2010 monograph,\u00a0<em>Rome's World: the Peutinger Map Reconsidered.</em></p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Stratonicidi is a place name included in the Peutinger map. It is situated in the Nile River Delta area. The place name is included in the manuscript, but there is no symbol associated with it.",
